            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0579" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg509"/>

                <head>No. 302.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 29, 1883</date>.
                        (Received June 30.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith for
                    your perusal copies of two reports of a committee of the privy council of Canada
                    relative to Indian raids, which have been communicated to me by the Marquis of
                    Lorne.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>







